# Glory Boxing Manager - Cursor AI Rules

## Project Context
- Boxing management simulation game
- Tech stack: Next.js 14, Supabase, Tailwind, ShadCN, OpenAI/OpenRouter
- Database: PostgreSQL with Realtime subscriptions
- AI Features: Voice generation, portrait creation, match commentary

## Code Patterns
- Use Supabase Edge Functions for AI integrations
- Store media (audio/images) in Supabase Storage
- Use Zustand for game state management
- Implement real-time updates for match results
- Follow ShadCN component patterns for UI

## Database Schema Focus
- fighters table (stats, portraits, voice_profile)
- matches table (results, commentary_audio)
- press_quotes table (text, audio_url)
- Use proper foreign keys and RLS policies
